o +5.2. White's reply H1 then lost 29.5, and the lead snapped back to +34.7. Neither side held the advantage for even one move."}, {"turn": 50, "text": "With Black's stones at A1, B1 and C1 and the lead at +2.6, GPT-6.1 Sol passed. That lost 34.1 points and was the worst move of the game. The engine's choice was E2, and Black played E2 on the next move to close the game at +36.6."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script is a helper: `inspect` parses the board and lists chains, liberties and borders, `candidate` computes the effect of one hand-picked move, and the later calls play moves, replay the game log to check it against the final board, and write notes. Nothing loops over empty points to score them or plays continuations forward, and the `allocation` list is a hand-edited set of points rather than a search.", "stop": false}}